WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.781
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.081 --> 00:00:14.973
Unit seventeen: Interviews. In this unit, you will ask and answer interview questions politely.

4
00:00:15.983 --> 00:00:16.868
Interview.

5
00:00:17.568 --> 00:00:21.367
Interview means a meeting where one person asks another person questions.

6
00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.644
I did an interview with my grandmother.

7
00:00:24.344 --> 00:00:26.810
Your turn. Say: Interview.

8
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:30.372
Interview.

9
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:32.210
Question.

10
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.898
Question means something you ask.

11
00:00:35.198 --> 00:00:37.035
I prepared five questions.

12
00:00:37.735 --> 00:00:40.446
Your turn. Say: Question.

13
00:00:43.146 --> 00:00:43.973
Question.

14
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:45.822
Answer.

15
00:00:46.522 --> 00:00:48.847
Answer means what you say back to a question.

16
00:00:49.147 --> 00:00:51.065
Her answer was very interesting.

17
00:00:51.765 --> 00:00:53.906
Your turn. Say: Answer.

18
00:00:56.606 --> 00:00:57.514
Answer.

19
00:00:58.517 --> 00:00:59.518
Interviewer.

20
00:01:00.218 --> 00:01:03.042
Interviewer means the person who asks the questions.

21
00:01:03.342 --> 00:01:05.515
The interviewer smiled and said hello.

22
00:01:06.215 --> 00:01:08.798
Your turn. Say: Interviewer.

23
00:01:11.498 --> 00:01:12.534
Interviewer.

24
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:14.354
Record.

25
00:01:15.054 --> 00:01:18.354
Record means to save sound or video to listen to later.

26
00:01:18.654 --> 00:01:20.769
I recorded the interview on my phone.

27
00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:23.913
Your turn. Say: Record.

28
00:01:26.613 --> 00:01:27.451
Record.

29
00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.381
Notes.

30
00:01:30.081 --> 00:01:32.824
Notes means short pieces of writing to help you remember.

31
00:01:33.124 --> 00:01:34.973
I took notes during the interview.

32
00:01:35.673 --> 00:01:37.919
Your turn. Say: Notes.

33
00:01:40.619 --> 00:01:41.620
Notes.

34
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:43.455
Polite.

35
00:01:44.155 --> 00:01:46.050
Polite means having good manners.

36
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.129
Be polite and say thank you.

37
00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:51.261
Your turn. Say: Polite.

38
00:01:53.961 --> 00:01:54.811
Polite.

39
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:56.644
Listen.

40
00:01:57.344 --> 00:02:00.051
Listen means to pay attention to sounds or words.

41
00:02:00.351 --> 00:02:02.455
Listen carefully to every answer.

42
00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.088
Your turn. Say: Listen.

43
00:02:07.788 --> 00:02:08.510
Listen.

44
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:11.447
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:11.747 --> 00:02:14.478
Sreypich, I hear you interviewed your grandfather.

46
00:02:15.783 --> 00:02:18.253
Yes! I asked, 'When were you born?'

47
00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.062
What else did you ask?

48
00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.562
'What was school like?' and 'Why did you become a farmer?'

49
00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.165
Did you take notes?

50
00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.472
Yes, and I recorded it. I listened politely to every answer.

51
00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:38.223
Grammar focus: Question forms (What and When and Why).

52
00:02:38.523 --> 00:02:41.349
When were you born? Why did you become a farmer?

53
00:02:41.649 --> 00:02:46.180
What asks about things, When asks about time, and Why asks for a reason.

54
00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:50.230
Now read and listen. Interviewing My Grandfather.

55
00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.739
For homework, I interviewed my grandfather.

56
00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.529
I asked, 'When were you born?' and 'What did you do as a child?'

57
00:02:58.817 --> 00:03:00.863
I recorded the interview and took notes.

58
00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.289
I listened politely and didn't interrupt him.

59
00:03:05.583 --> 00:03:08.767
I learned a lot about life in Cambodia in the past.

60
00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:12.678
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:12.978 --> 00:03:14.304
blank were you born?

62
00:03:14.604 --> 00:03:17.410
A, When. B, What. C, Who.

63
00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:23.730
The answer is A: When.

64
00:03:25.217 --> 00:03:27.762
The person who asks the questions is the blank.

65
00:03:28.062 --> 00:03:31.739
A, interviewer. B, answer. C, listener.

66
00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.657
The answer is A: interviewer.

67
00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.136
To save sound or video to listen to later is to blank.

68
00:03:42.436 --> 00:03:45.730
A, record. B, send. C, reply.

69
00:03:49.717 --> 00:03:51.972
The answer is A: record.

70
00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:57.831
Now it's your turn to speak. If you interview an older person, what will you ask?

71
00:04:03.131 --> 00:04:08.456
I will ask, 'When were you born?' and 'What was school like?' I will listen politely and take notes.

72
00:04:08.756 --> 00:04:10.616
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:16.405
Great work today! You learned eight new words and question forms (what and when and why).

74
00:04:16.705 --> 00:04:20.600
Today's value is respect for elders. Listen to and help older people.

75
00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.517
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:23.817 --> 00:04:26.621
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

